+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry validates tool input against the definition supplied to the provider.
+
+## Contract
+
+- The registry rejects missing required fields, wrong types and invalid enum values before executing a tool, returning a descriptive result without logging or returning values; accepted input including extra properties passes through unchanged, and an unknown tool still throws ([validated by: rejects invalid input before execution without exposing values and preserves valid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+- A static schema is compiled at registration, rejecting invalid schemas with the tool name, and reused for subsequent executions ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L52)).
+- A function-valued definition is validated against its currently resolved schema on each call ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
